# Extra chain certificates for https://eaindustry.nic.in ONLY. Chain building, never a trust anchor.
#
# Why: on 2026-10-28 eaindustry.nic.in renewed to a Let's Encrypt leaf issued by YR1 and now serves
# the leaf alone (`openssl s_client` verify error 21). Browsers fetch the missing issuer through the
# leaf's AIA URL; Python/OpenSSL does not, so the WPI capture failed CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED on
# 2026-10-29. YR1's issuer, ISRG Root YR, is not in certifi 2026.07.22 (nor the system store), so
# ISRG Root X1's cross-signature of Root YR is pinned too: the chain then ends at ISRG Root X1, a
# root certifi already carries. Owner approved this design on 2026-10-29.
#
# Neither certificate is self-signed (dataplatform/ingest/tls.py refuses one that is), and that
# module clears VERIFY_X509_PARTIAL_CHAIN, so OpenSSL accepts a chain only when it ends at a
# self-signed root already in certifi. Hostname checking stays on. Scope: the source register's
# `tls_extra_chain` on host eaindustry.nic.in, mounted for https://eaindustry.nic.in and nothing
# else; the loader checks both fingerprints below against the register before using this file.
#
# REVIEW BY 2027-01-26 (the leaf's expiry; a fetcher built after it logs
# fetch.tls_extra_chain_review_overdue). Delete this file and the register entry once certifi ships
# ISRG Root YR, or once the site serves its own chain; otherwise re-verify and extend review_by.
#
# [1] subject  C=US, O=Let's Encrypt, CN=YR1
#     issuer   C=US, O=ISRG, CN=Root YR
#     expires  2028-09-02 23:59:59 UTC (2028-09-03 05:29:59 IST)
#     SHA-256  13:94:96:34:D9:9C:D6:FD:6A:A8:0B:C0:34:FE:FA:CC:EB:19:69:FE:EF:98:65:86:71:3E:CD:BB:05:75:8D:3F
#     sources  http://yr1.i.lencr.org/ (AIA "CA Issuers" of the eaindustry.nic.in leaf) and
#              https://letsencrypt.org/certs/gen-y/int-yr1.pem, byte-identical, fetched 2026-10-29
